p=Path('DISAPPEARING-PURGE-AUTHORITY.md'); t=p.read_text(); add='''### Attachment Storage extension — 0.9.9.19 repository candidate\n\nThe single server purge repository is extended to Firebase Storage rather than introducing a second purge owner. For an eligible source it derives the deterministic encrypted-object prefix from server-visible authority (`senderUid`, conversation/group ID, message ID), revalidates the complete existing Firestore basis before the first physical mutation, deletes that Storage prefix with Admin Storage, then revalidates the same basis again before executing the existing Firestore trace/source commit. The source Firestore message remains the final source trace deleted. Text sources safely exercise an empty prefix; attachment sources remove manifest/chunks without server decryption of the E2EE descriptor. The live repository instantiation requires an injected Admin Storage bucket. The UID-scoped local-purge owner releases matching attachment object URLs/runtime records only after authoritative source absence. There is still no browser Storage delete authority, expired marker, tombstone, second scheduler, or second Firebase owner. Live activation requires explicit IAM/deployment handoff and device acceptance.\n\n'''
if '### Attachment Storage extension — 0.9.9.19' not in t: p.write_text(add+t)

